<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Batanaea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Batanaea was a region east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-galilee">Sea of Galilee</a> and north of the Yarmuk River, in present-day southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, corresponding to part of biblical Bashan. Augustus granted it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> in the 20s BCE, and it was later ruled by Philip the Tetrarch and the last Herodian kings. Herod settled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> there to guard the frontier.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/batanaea.jpg" alt="Batanaea" width="320" height="343" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: nl:Gebruiker:Machaerus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iturea-Trachonitis.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
